# Public Comms UX (workshop + consistency)

Companion to [`responsive-layouts.mdc`](responsive-layouts.mdc), [`public-marketing-ux.mdc`](public-marketing-ux.mdc) (Home / marketing effort bar), [`tool-editor-ux.mdc`](tool-editor-ux.mdc), and [`comms-module.mdc`](comms-module.mdc). Prefer **revising stale notes** when they block intentional responsive compositions — keep `PAGE_SHELL` tiers unless a change is documented here.

## Product language (lock)

| Prefer | Avoid on public Comms |
|--------|------------------------|
| **UnionOps Comms** / “this site” / named tool | Ambiguous “the hub” (confused with Officer Hub) — guarded in `public-copy-style.test.ts` |
| **Officer Hub** only for `/app` casework | Mixing Hub ops jargon into public tool chrome |
| **Brand Kit** + “Open Brand Kit” | “Start onboarding” once theme exists |
| **Graphic Maker**, **Image Resizer** | Divergent H1 vs nav (“News & Event…”, “Omnichannel…”) |
| **First week** roadmap | Multiple names for the same path without linking |

Use `brandSetupHref(themeEstablished)` from `@/lib/utils/brand-setup` (`/onboarding` until established, else `/brand-kit`). Shared nudge: [`BrandSetupPrompt`](src/components/tools/BrandSetupPrompt.tsx) (defaults to `common.setupBrandPrompt` / `common.setupBrandLink`).

**Collection profiles:** one Local identity by default; OPSEU preset is the only two-profile default (College Support Full-time / Part-time). Do not put CAAT FT/PT language in generic Brand Kit chrome. Rule + sources: [`brand-kit-collections.mdc`](brand-kit-collections.mdc).

## Copy style (public Comms)

- **Tool subtitles / guide intros:** one job each. Prefer ~12–18 words on subtitles; max two short sentences on intros. Put print tips and cross-links in hints, `whenToUse`, or related chips — not the lead line.
- **Body copy is not a lead.** Guide paragraphs, tips, checklist items, and hints should read as complete sentences a steward could say aloud. Do **not** clip subjects/verbs to hit a word count ("Prefer Install when it appears." is a failure, not a win). There is intentionally **no blanket per-leaf word ceiling** — the [`public-copy-style.test.ts`](../../src/lib/comms/public-copy-style.test.ts) guard only keeps a few *named* lead fields short and caps em-dash stacking on leads. Clarity beats brevity below the lead line.
- **Em dashes:** fine within reason for contrast (`Aid only — not legal advice`) or a single clause break. Do not stack multiple em dashes in one string, and prefer a period or colon in tool subtitles and home chrome when a dash only adds pause.
- **Error / empty / success states owe a consequence and a remedy.** Name the likely cause and the next action ("That file is not a Brand Kit export. Pick the .json file you downloaded from Brand Kit and try again."), not just the failure.
- Keep EN/FR in lockstep for every public string you change — and read the other locale's value, not just its key. French is a second source of truth that can be **wrong**, not a mirror. Full contract, locked French term names, banned jargon list, and the guard commands: [`i18n-public-copy.mdc`](i18n-public-copy.mdc).

## Workshop journey

1. Brand Kit / onboarding → identity  
2. First week: boards → print → socials → website ([`first-week-roadmap.ts`](src/lib/comms/first-week-roadmap.ts))  
3. Live demos: [`WorkshopDemoPath`](src/components/comms/WorkshopDemoPath.tsx) (Brand Kit → Board Notice → Graphic Maker → Captions). The numbered pitch stays on home / First week / workshop. Graphic Maker and Captions show a quiet `variant="trail"` continuation after a Demo Path click, a First week CTA to those tools, or the home hero Brand Kit / Get started button (tab session) — do not restamp “Demo this in about 20 minutes” on the tools. Header Brand Kit and Print / Website CTAs stay ordinary.  
4. Facilitator docs: [`docs/guides/WORKSHOP_SOCIAL_COMMS.md`](../../docs/guides/WORKSHOP_SOCIAL_COMMS.md); public outline: `/guide/workshop`; orientation: `/guide/resources`
5. Post-talk backlog / fit notes: [`docs/audit/workshop-gap-fit-2026-08.md`](../../docs/audit/workshop-gap-fit-2026-08.md)
6. Session lessons (merge hygiene, BrandSetup toolbar, PowerShell `@smoke`): [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-09-workshop-comms.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-09-workshop-comms.md)
7. Copy/i18n lessons (FR meaning errors, locked-term drift, mechanical-edit fingerprints): [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md)

## Tool chrome contracts

- Canvas tools: [`ToolEditorLayout`](src/components/tools/ToolEditorLayout.tsx) — sticky asymmetric preview at `lg`/`xl`; mobile Edit/Preview with **`aria-controls`** / panel ids; optional `purposeHint` (“when to use”); `exportError` + **`exportSuccess`** via [`useExportHandler`](src/hooks/use-export-handler.ts).
- Cross-links: [`ToolRelatedFooter`](src/components/tools/ToolRelatedFooter.tsx) / `RELATED_BY_TOOL` — add entries when shipping a new public tool.
- Tools index: one-line `toolsIndex.blurbs.*` per nav key; densify grids at `sm`/`lg`/`xl`.
- Captions page chrome and template bodies are i18n (`captions.*` / `captions.templates.*`); keep `#LocalUnion` + `[Local Number]` placeholders — avoid hardcoded national-union hashtags (`#OPSEU`). Per-union caption packs remain future scope.

## Responsive

Spot-check **375 / 768 / 1280 / 1536**. Re-touch surfaces marked “done” in [`tool-editor-ux.mdc`](tool-editor-ux.mdc) when the four-width check fails. Document-generator / alt-text remain layout exceptions — still reduce mobile scroll friction when touching those pages.

**Home:** must pass the two-zone / no-empty-half check in [`public-marketing-ux.mdc`](public-marketing-ux.mdc) and [`responsive-layouts.mdc`](responsive-layouts.mdc). Revising `HomeContent` is allowed when that fails — “landing shipped” in backlog docs is not a freeze.

## Do not

- Leak env vars, cron paths, or `*_DB_BACKEND` into public tool/guide copy for volunteers  
- Hardcode OPSEU/CAAT as the only local identity in new workshop copy  
- Invent one-off `max-w-*` page shells — use `PageShell` / `PAGE_SHELL`
